{"author":{"id":"5698b6d16d951325374257d86a2e673da0e55970c3d21c0f7c6f49018f24e5bf"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1786514934,"nonce":"NUW+AxFUsSevwB3/57e+cAEhT6k=","title":"**What is wrong.** `ViewService.links` builds three Alertmanager UI URLs by concatenating stock Alertmanager paths onto `snap.Group.AlertmanagerURL`, and it never asks what kind of source that URL came from. `internal/notification/service/view.go:402-410` trims the trailing slash and writes `base + \"/#/alerts?filter=\"` (`:405`), `base + \"/#/silences/new?filter=\"` (`:406`) and `base + \"/#/alerts\"` (`:408`). `AlertmanagerURL` is the source's `base_url` verbatim — `internal/notification/domain/snapshot.go:89-92` says so (\"AlertmanagerURL is the source's `base_url`. It is what the Silence and \\\"Open in Alertmanager\\\" deep links are built from (§H.3, R3)\"), and `groupFactsSQL` in `internal/notification/repository/snapshot.go:49-58` selects `coalesce(s.base_url,'')` at `:54` through `LEFT JOIN alert_sources s ON s.id = g.source_id` at `:57`. That join reads one column and stops; `s.kind` is never selected, so the kind is not merely unconsulted — it is not in the snapshot at all.","message":"**The demonstration.** `base_url` is documented as the ALERTMANAGER API ROOT, not a UI root: SPEC §D's DDL comments it `-- Alertmanager root, no trailing slash` (`docs/design/SPEC.md:817`). `alert_sources.kind` has two legal values, `CHECK (kind IN ('alertmanager','grafana'))` (`db/migrations/00004_sources.sql:59`), and `internal/sources/domain/source.go:15-20` spells them `KindAlertmanager` and `KindGrafana`.\n\nCommit c46a93f settled what that means for a deep link and wrote the reasoning into the composition root. `internal/app/silencesource.go:88-100`: *\"`base_url` is documented everywhere as the Alertmanager API root; for `KindAlertmanager` the API root and the UI root are the same origin, so `\u003cbase\u003e/#/silences/\u003cid\u003e` resolves. For `KindGrafana` neither half holds: the source factory appends stock `/api/v2/...` paths without ever reading Kind, so a grafana `base_url` must already carry Grafana's AM-compat prefix — and Grafana serves its silences at `/alerting/silences`, not at `/#/silences`. Whichever way an operator configured it, the link would be wrong.\"* `silenceBaseURLs.BaseURLs` acts on it in four lines: `if src.Kind != sourcesdomain.KindAlertmanager { continue }` (`internal/app/silencesource.go:110-112`), so a non-Alertmanager source is absent from the map and `internal/silences/api/silences.go:248` renders a null `alertmanager_url` rather than a fabricated one.\n\nThe notification renderer has no equivalent. Its three URLs are built for every source kind, and the second of them is a button an operator presses: `view.go:462-466` turns a non-empty `Links.AlertmanagerSilenceNew` into the Slack action `oto.noop.silence`, labelled \"Silence\". For a `grafana` source the card therefore carries a Silence button and an \"Open in Alertmanager\" link pointed at `\u003cgrafana-AM-compat-root\u003e/#/silences/new?filter=…` and `\u003csame\u003e/#/alerts` — paths Grafana does not serve.\n\n**Why it matters.** SPEC R3 (`docs/design/SPEC.md:36`): *\"**Silences are a READ-ONLY mirror of Alertmanager silences in v1.** oto has NO write path into the cluster. The Slack \\\"Silence\\\" affordance is a **deep-link URL button** into the Alertmanager UI (zero API calls, zero state).\"* The code says the same thing about itself at `view.go:393-397` — *\"⛔ THE ONLY SILENCE AFFORDANCE v1 HAS (R3, §H.3) … Without it the card is missing the one action an operator reaches for at 03:00.\"* When that single affordance is a 404, the operator has spent the worst minute of their night proving oto wrong about the one thing it offered to do for them, and the fallback — hand-building the matcher — is exactly where they would have been with no button, minus the trust. The same commit already refused to ship that outcome on the silences list; the Slack card, which is the surface an operator actually sees first, still ships it.\n\n**Where.** `internal/notification/service/view.go:402-410` (the three URLs) and `:462-466` (the button they become); `internal/notification/domain/snapshot.go:89-92` (the field, documented as `base_url`); `internal/notification/repository/snapshot.go:49-58` (the join that already reaches `alert_sources` and takes one column from it); `internal/app/silencesource.go:85-116` (the precedent); `docs/design/SPEC.md:36` (R3), `:817` (`base_url` is the API root); `db/migrations/00004_sources.sql:59` (the two kinds).\n\n**Scope.** small\n\n**Done when.** `groupFactsSQL` also selects `s.kind`, `domain.GroupFacts` carries it, and `links` builds `Alertmanager` and `AlertmanagerSilenceNew` only when the source is `alertmanager` — leaving both empty otherwise, which `actions` (`view.go:462`) already renders as no Silence button and the card already renders as no link. The precedent to follow is the silences path: `silenceBaseURLs.BaseURLs` (`internal/app/silencesource.go:101-116`) makes kind the filter, makes absence the answer, and lets the layer above render nothing rather than something wrong — the notification renderer should reach the same verdict by the same route. A test pins that a snapshot whose source is `grafana` yields an empty `Links.AlertmanagerSilenceNew` and no `oto.noop.silence` action, so the guard cannot be removed silently.","files":null}]}